    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0423" n="1177" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.96/83a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5812. For McCormick from
                    War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>7. Since your departure Swiss have submitted suggested agreement differing in
                    substance as well as form from one worked out by Taylor. We are convinced Swiss
                    agreement should be negotiated and concluded by you and Taylor in Paris in conference
                    with committees there with full knowledge of the situation. Grimprel and
                        Percy<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d301-f1"/> coincide with this view. Prompt answer necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d301-f1" n="2" xml:id="d301-f1-content">
                <p>Temporarily attached to the French and British Embassies, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
